## Findings
1. blocking — apps/web/src/screens/Inbox.tsx:125 [severity: S1] Reconciliation equates a retained `attentionKey` with a retained decision. If an ordinary refresh removes the drafted petition but leaves another question, Greenlight, or Human gate on the same opus, `keepDetached` is false and the reading pane silently replaces the draft instead of preserving it as withdrawn, contrary to brief:79. — check: apps/web/tests-serve/w487.spec.ts b2: type a ratio on a mixed row, remove only its petition during an ordinary refresh while retaining its Board ask, and require the original draft with disabled withdrawn controls [class: tests×tests-that-agree-with-the-bug]
2. blocking — apps/web/src/screens/InboxView.tsx:177 [severity: S1] A detached petition derives `Open Board actions` from the fallback live `selectedItem`; when the removed petition is followed by a mixed row, its withdrawn detail exposes a clickable action for the other opus, violating brief:54’s preserved detached-reply interaction. — check: apps/web/test/w407.test.ts: render a detached petition beside a mixed replacement item and require no Board action until that live item is selected [class: tests×one-sided-bound-assertion]
3. blocking — apps/web/src/App.tsx:100 [severity: S1] The mounted-screen short-circuit retains the shell’s previous nonzero count, while first-load failures in Inbox or Board never report zero. Navigating from a successfully counted Officina/Seats screen into a failing Inbox or Board therefore leaves both badges nonzero although the mounted collection is empty, contrary to brief:52. — check: apps/web/tests-serve/w487.spec.ts b4: seed a nonzero off-screen count, hash-navigate without reload, fail the mounted screen’s first reconciliation, and require both badges hidden [class: tests×one-sided-bound-assertion]

